-- VIVA QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS (HINGLISH)
-- =========================================

-- Q1. What is a trigger in PL/SQL?
-- Ans: Trigger ek stored PL/SQL block hai jo
-- specified database event par automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q2. What is the purpose of EMP_INSERT_AUDIT?
-- Ans: Is table mein employee ki insertion date aur
-- database username ke saath details store hoti hain.

-- Q3. What does AFTER INSERT mean?
-- Ans: Naya employee insert hone ke baad trigger execute hota hai.

-- Q4. What is :NEW?
-- Ans: :NEW insert ya update hone wali row ki new values
-- access karne ke liye use hota hai.

-- Q5. What is SYSDATE?
-- Ans: SYSDATE database server ki current date aur time return karta hai.

-- Q6. What does USER return?
-- Ans: USER current Oracle database session ka username return karta hai.

-- Q7. Why is FOR EACH ROW used?
-- Ans: Isse trigger har inserted employee row ke liye execute hota hai.

-- Q8. Does a trigger need to be called manually?
-- Ans: Nahi, INSERT statement execute hone par trigger automatically fire hota hai.

-- Q9. What is an audit table?
-- Ans: Audit table database activities ka record maintain karti hai.

-- Q10. What is the purpose of COMMIT?
-- Ans: COMMIT transaction ke changes permanently save karta hai.

-- Q11. What happens if the INSERT statement fails?
-- Ans: Agar employee insert nahi hota, to us row ke liye
-- trigger ka audit insert bhi successfully nahi hota.

-- Q12. What is the difference between SYSDATE and USER?
-- Ans: SYSDATE date aur time deta hai, jabki USER
-- current Oracle database username deta hai.

-- Q13. What is the purpose of SHOW ERRORS?
-- Ans: Isse trigger compile karte waqt aayi errors check kar sakte hain.

-- Q14. Can one trigger store data in another table?
-- Ans: Haan, trigger ke andar INSERT statement use karke
-- doosri table mein audit data store kar sakte hain.

-- Q15. What is the difference between BEFORE and AFTER triggers?
-- Ans: BEFORE trigger operation se pehle aur AFTER trigger
-- operation ke baad execute hota hai.
